/// Decides when an agent's conversation should start afresh, and says so by
/// publishing a new conversation epoch.
///
/// Each new message on `interactions` counts as one interaction and moves the
/// idle clock. A message on `activity` only moves the idle clock; it counts
/// nothing. `tick` is the component's self-timer: while anything is counted it
/// keeps one wake parked there, and it parks nothing while the count is zero.
/// A fire publishes a fresh decimal epoch on `epoch`, one higher than the last,
/// and resets the count.
///
/// It fires when either rule holds: at least one interaction and `idle_secs`
/// of quiet since the last activity, or at least `max_interactions`
/// interactions and `settle_secs` of quiet. The three `config` keys are whole
/// numbers and default to `idle_secs = "180"`, `max_interactions = "50"` and
/// `settle_secs = "10"`; a value that does not parse, or a `max_interactions`
/// of zero, fails the activation naming the key.
///
/// Its `store` keeps the count, the idle clock, a per-port high-water mark of
/// the newest publish time it has counted, and the epoch generation, so a
/// re-attach that redelivers the retained tail neither re-counts it nor
/// restarts the idle clock, and the epoch keeps rising across restarts.
component ConversationRecycler {
  abi = processor;
  requires = [ports, store, log, config];
  in interactions;
  optional in activity;
  io tick;
  out epoch: "brenn.conversation.epoch@1";
}
